DOCUMENTATION_STANDARD_VERSION 0.1.0

STATUS DRAFT

OWNER President Cley Duarte

SCOPE ORGANIZATION

DEPENDS_ON

protocols/LEARNING_PROTOCOL_0.1.0.pdl (promoted from a REQUEST through
  that protocol)
standards/PROJECT_MANAGEMENT_STANDARD_0.1.0.pdl (same tool, ClickUp: that
  standard governs how work is tracked, this one governs where produced
  documents live)

PURPOSE

Fix where an AI puts the documentation and presentations it produces for a
governed project: when the ROOT_AUTHORITY wants them, they are created in
ClickUp — not left as scattered local files or trapped inside a chat.

TRIGGER

This standard is OPT-IN, at the ROOT_AUTHORITY's choice. The AI does not
generate ClickUp documentation on its own initiative. It does so when the
ROOT_AUTHORITY asks for documentation or a presentation, or has given a
standing instruction to. Absent that, the AI only proposes it.

WHERE

  Documentation  A ClickUp DOC inside the project's own folder (the same
                 folder defined by the Project-Management Standard).
                 Multi-part documentation uses pages within that Doc.

  Presentations  A ClickUp DOC as well, structured as a deck (one page or
                 section per slide), so it lives beside the project's
                 other views and stays editable in place. If an exported
                 file (for example a .pptx) is also required, it is
                 produced in addition, never instead.

LOCATION_AND_DISCOVERABILITY

So documentation and presentations are always found the same way, without
anyone ever being reminded where they are, their location is fixed by
convention — not chosen per project:

  - They live in the project's own ClickUp FOLDER, under its Docs.
  - The project documentation is a single Doc named
    "PROJECT — Documentacion del Proyecto" (emoji prefix allowed).
  - Presentations are Docs in the same folder, named
    "PROJECT — TITLE" with a distinct emoji prefix so they are told
    apart from the documentation at a glance.

An AI applies this convention automatically for every governed project. It
does not ask where to put documentation, and it does not ask where to find
it — the folder and the naming are always the same.

CORRESPONDENCE

ClickUp holds the human-facing, editable document. Any lasting knowledge
inside it (a decision, a policy, a lesson) is still recorded into .pace/
as the appropriate entity — the Doc is the presentation surface, .pace/ is
the memory of record.

ORIGIN

Promoted from REQUEST-0003 (2026-07-25): the ROOT_AUTHORITY directed that
PACE's structure must indicate that the AI, when the user wants it, creates
documentation and presentations in ClickUp. Refined by REQUEST-0004
(2026-07-25): the location must be fixed and discoverable so it is applied
automatically across all projects, without reminding.

END
